    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d256">

                <pb facs="0685" n="635" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv12/pg635"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 181.92/3: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Commission to Negotiate Peace</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-07-25T18:00:00-04:00">July 25, 1919—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 26—10 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>2636. Your 3231 and 3222 [<hi rendition="#italic">3232?</hi>] and 3239.<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d256-f1"/> President has approved that army officer be
                    detailed to represent the United States on mission to Hungary. General Bliss may
                    make the selection from list which he has.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
